cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this software in work you publish, please cite it, and cite the
  papers whose algorithms it implements — they are listed under `references`.
title: "vol-surface: SABR and SVI implied-volatility calibration with Gatheral-Jacquier arbitrage checks"
abstract: >-
  A pure-Python library for fitting implied-volatility smiles and surfaces.
  It provides Black-Scholes pricing and Greeks, a bracketed Brent implied-vol
  solver, Hagan's SABR expansion, raw SVI calibrated by the De Marco/Martini
  quasi-explicit reduction, and multi-expiry surfaces stitched in total
  variance. Every fitted slice is checked against the Gatheral-Jacquier
  butterfly condition and every surface against calendar monotonicity, and
  discrete model-free screens are provided for raw quotes. The package imports
  only the Python standard library; its results are validated against external
  references in docs/validation.md.
type: software
